 <skos:definition xml:lang='en'>Wikipedia: Ureases (EC 3.5.1.5), belong to the superfamily of amidohydrolases and catalyzes the hydrolysis of urea Wikipedia: into carbon dioxide and ammonia: (NH2)2CO + H2O &#8594; CO2 + 2 NH3.</skos:definition>
 <skos:definition xml:lang='fr'>Wikipedia: L&apos;ur&#233;ase  (EC 3.5.1.5)est une enzyme de la famille des  amidohydrolases qui catalyse la r&#233;action de transformation de l&apos;ur&#233;e en dioxyde de carbone et ammoniac&#160;: (NH2)2CO + H2O &#8594; CO2 + 2 NH3.</skos:definition>
 <skos:inScheme rdf:resource='http://opendata.inra.fr/anaeeThes/'/>
 <skos:prefLabel xml:lang='fr'>ur&#233;ase</skos:prefLabel>
 <skos:prefLabel xml:lang='en'>urease</skos:prefLabel>
 <skos:scopeNote xml:lang='en'>mU/g dry soil</skos:scopeNote>
 <skos:scopeNote xml:lang='fr'>mU/g sol sec</skos:scopeNote>
</rdf:Description>

