 <skos:definition xml:lang='en'>A CompositeUnit is a product at least two base or derived units. For example, &apos;meter per second square&apos; denotes a composite unit defined over &apos;meter&apos; (a base unit) and &apos;per second square&apos; (a derived unit).</skos:definition>
