 <skos:broader rdf:resource='http://opendata.inra.fr/anaeeThes/c2_2882'/>
 <skos:definition xml:lang='en'>Groundwater is found in two zones. The unsaturated zone, immediately below the land surface, contains water and air in the open spaces, or pores. The saturated zone, a zone in which all the pores and rock fractures are filled with water, underlies the unsaturated zone. The top of the saturated zone is called the water table (http://www.epa.gov/superfund/students/clas_act/haz-ed/ff_05.htm)</skos:definition>
 <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource='http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_16075'/>
 <skos:inScheme rdf:resource='http://opendata.inra.fr/anaeeThes/'/>
 <skos:prefLabel xml:lang='en'>groundwater table</skos:prefLabel>
</rdf:Description>

