 <skos:definition xml:lang='en'>Unit of pressures often used in meteorology. One hectopascal is equivalent to one millibar; one standard atmosphere is exactly equal to 1013.25 hPa. One hectopascal corresponds to about 0.1% of atmospheric pressure near sea level (Wikipedia).</skos:definition>
