 <skos:definition xml:lang='en'>a very large and widespread family of monocotyledoneae with more than 10 000 species most of which are herbaceous but a few are woody the stems are jointed the long narrow leaves originating at the nodes the flowers are inconspicuous with a much reduced perianth and are wind pollinated or cleistogamous the fruit in single seeded usually a caryopsis grasses are the most important of all plants for food</skos:definition>
 <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource='http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_3362'/>
 <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource='http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/3729'/>
